# AICL Example: Feature Store
# Production feature store implementing feature computation, online/offline serving,
# feature versioning, lineage tracking, and point-in-time correctness for ML workloads.

Goal Build a production feature store that provides unified feature computation, dual online and offline serving paths, feature versioning with lineage tracking, and guaranteed point-in-time correctness to prevent training-serving skew in ML systems

Constraint Point-in-time feature retrieval must guarantee no data leakage for any lookback window
Constraint Online serving latency must remain below 5ms p99 for single entity feature lookups
Constraint Offline serving must support batch scans of billions of entity-feature rows
Constraint Feature versioning must maintain full lineage from raw data to feature value
Constraint Feature computation must be deterministic and reproducible given same input data

Risk Training-serving skew from inconsistent feature computation between offline and online paths
Recovery Implement shared computation logic between online and offline paths; deploy feature verification pipeline that compares online and offline feature distributions; auto-alert on distribution divergence exceeding threshold

Risk Point-in-time correctness violation from late-arriving data
Recovery Implement event-time processing with watermark tracking; reject data arriving after watermark threshold; maintain late-data correction queue; validate no future data leaks into training features

Risk Online feature store hotspot causing read latency spikes
Recovery Implement consistent hashing for key distribution; deploy read replicas with async replication; enable local caching with TTL for hot entities; scale shards dynamically on load

Risk Feature computation failure leaving stale values in online store
Recovery Implement staleness detection with TTL-based validation; fall back to last-known-good feature values on computation failure; alert on stale features and trigger recomputation; maintain feature health dashboard

Risk Feature version conflict during concurrent updates
Recovery Use optimistic locking with version stamps on feature writes; implement conflict resolution with last-writer-wins and notification; maintain write-ahead log for recovery; enforce serialized writes for critical features

Risk Lineage gap preventing reproducibility of feature values
Recovery Require lineage metadata for all feature writes; validate lineage chain completeness on read; block feature registration without upstream lineage; audit lineage gaps periodically

Layer FeatureComputation
    SubLayer: TransformationEngine
    SubLayer: AggregationEngine
    SubLayer: EnrichmentEngine
Layer FeatureServing
    SubLayer: OnlineStore
    SubLayer: OfflineStore
    SubLayer: ServingAPI
Layer FeatureGovernance
    SubLayer: VersionControl
    SubLayer: LineageTracker
    SubLayer: QualityMonitor
    SubLayer: AccessControl

Validation Point-in-time retrieval must produce identical features to historical offline values for any timestamp
Validation Online serving latency must remain below 5ms p99 under 50K QPS load
Validation Offline serving must scan 1 billion rows within 30 minutes on standard cluster
Validation Feature computation determinism must be verified via checksum comparison across runs
Validation Training-serving skew must be detected when online/offline feature PSI exceeds 0.1
Validation Lineage chain must be traceable from any feature value back to raw data source
Validation Feature version changes must not break existing consumers without migration period
Validation Staleness detection must flag any feature value older than configured TTL

# Level 2 - Entities

Entity FeatureDefinition
    featureId: string
    featureName: string
    featureGroup: string
    featureType: string
    transformLogic: string
    sourceFeatures: list
    entityKey: string
    defaultValue: any
    validityRange: dict
    stalenessTtl: string
    version: string
    owner: string
    description: string

Entity FeatureValue
    featureId: string
    entityId: string
    value: any
    timestamp: datetime
    version: string
    lineageId: string
    isValid: boolean
    computedAt: datetime
    sourceChecksum: string

Entity FeatureGroup
    groupId: string
    groupName: string
    entityKey: string
    features: list
    computationSchedule: string
    onlineEnabled: boolean
    offlineEnabled: boolean
    ttl: string
    version: string
    owner: string
    createdAt: datetime

Entity LineageRecord
    lineageId: string
    featureId: string
    entityId: string
    timestamp: datetime
    inputFeatureIds: list
    inputChecksums: dict
    transformVersion: string
    outputChecksum: string
    computationDuration: float
    source: string

Entity PointInTimeQuery
    queryId: string
    entityIds: list
    featureIds: list
    timestamp: datetime
    lookbackWindow: string
    resultFormat: string
    includeLineage: boolean
    submittedAt: datetime
    completedAt: datetime

Entity FeatureStatistics
    statId: string
    featureId: string
    version: string
    mean: float
    stddev: float
    min: float
    max: float
    nullCount: integer
    totalCount: integer
    percentile25: float
    percentile50: float
    percentile75: float
    computedAt: datetime

# Level 3 - Behaviors

Behavior ComputeFeature
    Input:
        featureDefinition: FeatureDefinition
        sourceData: dict
        computationConfig: dict
    Output:
        featureValue: FeatureValue
        lineageRecord: LineageRecord
    Action:
        Validate source data availability and checksums
        Apply transformation logic from feature definition
        Validate output against feature type and validity range
        Apply default value for null or invalid results
        Compute lineage record with input and output checksums
        Write feature value to online and offline stores
        Update feature statistics incrementally
        Return feature value with lineage metadata

Behavior ServeFeatureOnline
    Input:
        entityId: string
        featureIds: list
        servingConfig: dict
    Output:
        featureValues: dict
        stalenessReport: dict
        latencyMs: float
    Action:
        Look up feature values from online key-value store
        Check staleness TTL for each returned feature value
        For stale features, trigger async recomputation and return last-known-good
        Verify feature version compatibility
        Compute serving latency and track metrics
        Return feature values with staleness indicators

Behavior ServeFeatureOffline
    Input:
        pointInTimeQuery: PointInTimeQuery
        servingConfig: dict
    Output:
        featureDataset: dict
        queryMetrics: dict
    Action:
        Resolve feature definitions and versions for query
        Construct point-in-time join plan with entity and timestamp keys
        Apply lookback window constraints to prevent data leakage
        Execute batch scan against offline store with partition pruning
        Validate no future data leaks into result set
        Compute and return feature dataset with query metrics

Behavior VersionFeature
    Input:
        featureId: string
        newDefinition: FeatureDefinition
        versionConfig: dict
    Output:
        newVersion: string
        migrationReport: dict
    Action:
        Compare new definition against current version
        Identify breaking vs non-breaking changes
        Create new version entry in version control
        If breaking change, generate migration guide and deprecation timeline
        Validate compatibility with existing consumers
        Register new version with lineage linkage to previous
        Return new version with migration report

Behavior TrackLineage
    Input:
        featureValue: FeatureValue
        computationContext: dict
    Output:
        lineageRecord: LineageRecord
    Action:
        Record all input feature IDs and their checksums
        Record transform logic version used
        Compute output feature value checksum
        Link to upstream data source lineage records
        Store lineage record in lineage store
        Validate lineage chain completeness
        Return lineage record for audit trail

Behavior ValidateFeatureQuality
    Input:
        featureId: string
        expectedStatistics: FeatureStatistics
        actualData: list
    Output:
        qualityReport: dict
        anomalyDetected: boolean
    Action:
        Compute actual statistics from feature data sample
        Compare against expected distribution statistics
        Run KS-test and PSI for distribution drift detection
        Check null rate against configured threshold
        Validate value range against expected bounds
        Generate quality report with anomaly flags
        Return quality assessment with remediation suggestions

# Level 4 - Conditions

Condition: TrainingServingSkewDetected
    When PSI between online and offline feature distributions exceeds 0.1
    Then alert feature owners; trigger feature verification pipeline; block model training with skewed features; initiate root cause analysis

Condition: FeatureStalenessExceeded
    When feature value timestamp exceeds configured TTL
    Then flag feature as stale in online store; trigger priority recomputation; serve last-known-good with staleness warning; update staleness dashboard

Condition: PointInTimeLeakDetected
    When feature value timestamp is after query timestamp in point-in-time retrieval
    Then reject the leaked feature value; replace with null or default; log leak incident for investigation; validate watermark logic

Condition: FeatureVersionBreakingChange
    When feature version update involves type change or removal without migration
    Then block version deployment; require migration plan; notify all consumers; enforce deprecation timeline with minimum 30-day notice

Condition: ComputationFailurePersistence
    When feature computation fails for more than 3 consecutive scheduled runs
    Then escalate to feature owner; enable fallback to previous stable version; alert on-call team; maintain service with degraded feature set

# Level 5 - Events

Event: FeatureComputed
    On successful feature computation and storage
    Action: update online store; refresh statistics; emit computation metrics; notify dependent features

Event: FeatureStalenessAlert
    On feature value exceeding TTL threshold
    Action: trigger recomputation; update staleness dashboard; notify feature consumers; log staleness event

Event: SkewDetected
    On training-serving skew exceeding threshold
    Action: block affected model training; alert feature and ML teams; initiate verification pipeline; publish skew analysis report

Event: FeatureVersionRegistered
    On new feature version created in version control
    Action: validate backward compatibility; notify registered consumers; update documentation; schedule migration if needed

Event: LineageGapDetected
    On incomplete lineage chain discovered during audit
    Action: log lineage gap with affected features; alert data governance team; block feature usage until lineage restored; initiate manual lineage repair

# Level 6 - Concurrency

Parallel:
    Feature computation across independent feature groups simultaneously
    Online serving reads concurrent with background writes
    Offline batch scans across multiple partitions
    Statistics computation alongside feature serving
    Lineage tracking parallel with value computation
    Quality validation across multiple features concurrently

# Level 7 - Optimization

Optimize: Online serving latency
    Priority: Sub-5ms p99 latency; use in-memory key-value store; co-locate features by access pattern; pre-warm caches for active entities

Optimize: Offline scan throughput
    Priority: Maximize partition pruning; use columnar storage format; predicate pushdown on entity and timestamp; parallel scan across partitions

Optimize: Feature computation efficiency
    Priority: Share intermediate computation results across features; incremental aggregation for time-window features; batch entity computation; avoid redundant source reads

# Level 8 - Learning

Learn: Optimal feature staleness TTL per feature
    Goal: Set TTLs that minimize staleness incidents while reducing unnecessary recomputation
    Adapt: TTL values per feature based on update frequency
    Based: Staleness alert frequency, computation cost, and downstream impact metrics

Learn: Feature access patterns for cache optimization
    Goal: Maximize cache hit rates by predicting which features will be requested together
    Adapt: Cache grouping and pre-warming strategies
    Based: Historical feature access co-occurrence patterns and query logs

Learn: Computation schedule optimization
    Goal: Schedule feature computation to minimize staleness while reducing compute cost
    Adapt: Computation trigger intervals and batch sizes
    Based: Feature value change rates, access patterns, and staleness incident history

Learn: Quality anomaly detection thresholds
    Goal: Detect genuine quality issues while minimizing false positive alerts
    Adapt: Statistical thresholds for drift and anomaly detection per feature
    Based: Historical quality reports, false positive rates, and missed anomaly incidents

# Level 9 - Security

Security:
    Encrypt: Feature values at rest in online and offline stores using AES-256 with per-feature-group encryption keys
    Encrypt: Serving API communication with TLS 1.3 and API key authentication
    Protect: Feature definitions and transform logic from unauthorized modification via signed configuration
    Protect: Feature access with fine-grained RBAC scoped to feature groups and entity types
    Encrypt: Lineage records containing sensitive source information with field-level encryption
    Protect: Point-in-time query results with row-level security based on consumer permissions
    Protect: Feature statistics containing distribution information with aggregation-level access controls

# Level 10 - Native

Native: python
{
import hashlib
import json
from datetime import datetime, timedelta
from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Any, Tuple
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from collections import defaultdict

@dataclass
class PointInTimeJoin:
    lookback_window: timedelta = timedelta(days=30)

    def join_features(
        self,
        entity_df: List[Dict],
        feature_df: List[Dict],
        entity_key: str,
        timestamp_key: str,
        feature_timestamp_key: str
    ) -> List[Dict]:
        feature_index = defaultdict(list)
        for row in feature_df:
            key = row[entity_key]
            feature_index[key].append(row)

        result = []
        for entity_row in entity_df:
            entity_id = entity_row[entity_key]
            entity_ts = datetime.fromisoformat(entity_row[timestamp_key])
            merged = entity_row.copy()

            candidates = feature_index.get(entity_id, [])
            valid_candidates = [
                c for c in candidates
                if datetime.fromisoformat(c[feature_timestamp_key]) <= entity_ts
                and datetime.fromisoformat(c[feature_timestamp_key]) >= entity_ts - self.lookback_window
            ]

            if valid_candidates:
                latest = max(valid_candidates, key=lambda x: x[feature_timestamp_key])
                for k, v in latest.items():
                    if k not in merged and k != feature_timestamp_key:
                        merged[k] = v
                        merged[f"_{k}_timestamp"] = latest[feature_timestamp_key]

            result.append(merged)

        return result

@dataclass
class FeatureStore:
    online_store: Dict[str, Dict] = field(default_factory=dict)
    offline_store: List[Dict] = field(default_factory=list)
    feature_versions: Dict[str, List[Dict]] = field(default_factory=dict)
    lineage_store: List[Dict] = field(default_factory=list)
    statistics: Dict[str, Dict] = field(default_factory=dict)

    def write_online(self, entity_id: str, feature_group: str,
                     values: Dict[str, Any], timestamp: datetime) -> None:
        key = f"{feature_group}:{entity_id}"
        self.online_store[key] = {
            "values": values,
            "timestamp": timestamp.isoformat(),
            "version": self._get_current_version(feature_group)
        }

    def read_online(self, entity_id: str, feature_group: str) -> Optional[Dict]:
        key = f"{feature_group}:{entity_id}"
        return self.online_store.get(key)

    def write_offline(self, entity_id: str, feature_group: str,
                      values: Dict[str, Any], timestamp: datetime) -> None:
        record = {
            "entity_id": entity_id,
            "feature_group": feature_group,
            "values": values,
            "timestamp": timestamp.isoformat(),
            "version": self._get_current_version(feature_group)
        }
        self.offline_store.append(record)

    def record_lineage(self, feature_id: str, entity_id: str,
                       input_features: Dict[str, str],
                       transform_version: str) -> Dict:
        lineage = {
            "lineage_id": hashlib.sha256(
                f"{feature_id}:{entity_id}:{transform_version}".encode()
            ).hexdigest()[:16],
            "feature_id": feature_id,
            "entity_id": entity_id,
            "input_features": input_features,
            "transform_version": transform_version,
            "timestamp": datetime.utcnow().isoformat()
        }
        self.lineage_store.append(lineage)
        return lineage

    def compute_statistics(self, feature_id: str, values: List[Any]) -> Dict:
        numeric_values = [v for v in values if isinstance(v, (int, float))]
        if not numeric_values:
            return {"feature_id": feature_id, "null_count": len(values), "total": len(values)}

        sorted_vals = sorted(numeric_values)
        n = len(sorted_vals)
        mean = sum(sorted_vals) / n
        variance = sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in sorted_vals) / n

        stats = {
            "feature_id": feature_id,
            "mean": mean,
            "stddev": variance ** 0.5,
            "min": sorted_vals[0],
            "max": sorted_vals[-1],
            "null_count": len(values) - n,
            "total_count": len(values),
            "percentile25": sorted_vals[int(n * 0.25)],
            "percentile50": sorted_vals[int(n * 0.50)],
            "percentile75": sorted_vals[int(n * 0.75)],
            "computed_at": datetime.utcnow().isoformat()
        }
        self.statistics[feature_id] = stats
        return stats

    def _get_current_version(self, feature_group: str) -> str:
        versions = self.feature_versions.get(feature_group, [])
        return versions[-1]["version"] if versions else "v0"

@dataclass
class SkewDetector:
    psi_threshold: float = 0.1

    def detect_skew(self, offline_stats: Dict, online_stats: Dict) -> Dict:
        psi_values = {}
        skewed_features = []

        for feature_name in offline_stats:
            if feature_name not in online_stats:
                continue
            psi = self._compute_psi(
                offline_stats[feature_name].get("mean", 0),
                offline_stats[feature_name].get("stddev", 1),
                online_stats[feature_name].get("mean", 0),
                online_stats[feature_name].get("stddev", 1)
            )
            psi_values[feature_name] = psi
            if psi > self.psi_threshold:
                skewed_features.append(feature_name)

        return {
            "skew_detected": len(skewed_features) > 0,
            "skewed_features": skewed_features,
            "psi_values": psi_values,
            "threshold": self.psi_threshold
        }

    def _compute_psi(self, mean1: float, std1: float,
                     mean2: float, std2: float) -> float:
        import math
        if std1 <= 0 or std2 <= 0:
            return 0.0
        psi = math.log(std2 / std1) + (std1**2 + (mean1 - mean2)**2) / (2 * std2**2) - 0.5
        return max(0, psi)
}
